Z||000000||fropuff||06-02-2000||04:56 PM||||Hi.  I was wondering if anyone knows how to remove the molding off of my 86 GT.  When I open the door and look on the back side of the in side of the door, I can see that the molding is riveted to the body.  How to I get these pieces off?  Also, how do I remove the molding on the door.  Do I have to remove the door panels?  Are the molding pieces attached with clips or with clips and rivets?  Thanks.<P>P.S&gt;  Does anyone know how to remove the front fascia?  How do I get the body rivets out?  Thanks again.||||reg||4
Z||000001||Monkeyman||06-03-2000||11:14 AM||||I assume you're talking about the GT style molding at the bottom of the door since the belt line molding isn't riveted on.  I think there are some plastic rivet on the bottom.  If you remove these, you should be able to slide the molding up and off of the top clip.  That's the part that's riveted on, not the molding itself.  (Someone correct me if I'm wrong.  It's been a while since I dismantled a door.)||||reg||1
